      "syllabusTopic": "Institutional support: NABARD, SFAC, APEDA, MSME, and DIC roles",
      "questionText": "Summarize the salient features of the revised MSME classification criteria introduced in India in 2020.",
      "modelAnswer": "Under the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises Development (MSMED) Act, 2006, enterprises were historically classified separately for manufacturing and services based purely on historical investment ceilings in plant and machinery or equipment.\n\nIn July 2020, the Government of India enacted a historic revision, removing the artificial distinction between manufacturing and service sectors and introducing a unified, composite criteria framework combining capital investment and annual turnover:\n\n1. Revised Composite Thresholds:\n- Micro Enterprise: Investment in Plant and Machinery or Equipment does not exceed \u20b91 Crore, AND Annual Turnover does not exceed \u20b95 Crore.\n- Small Enterprise: Investment in Plant and Machinery or Equipment does not exceed \u20b910 Crore, AND Annual Turnover does not exceed \u20b950 Crore.\n- Medium Enterprise: Investment in Plant and Machinery or Equipment does not exceed \u20b950 Crore, AND Annual Turnover does not exceed \u20b9250 Crore.\n\n2. Salient Operational Features:\n- Composite Criterion Rule: If an enterprise crosses either the investment OR the turnover ceiling for its existing category, it is automatically elevated to the next higher classification bracket.\n- Export Turnover Exclusion: In calculating annual turnover for MSME status, revenue derived from foreign exports of goods or services is completely excluded. This incentivizes agri-exporters (such as basmati rice or spice processors) to expand export shipments without forfeiting MSME priority lending and subsidy benefits.\n- Paperless Udyam Registration: Classification is verified seamlessly through automated integration of Income Tax and GST data on the Udyam portal using PAN and Aadhaar.",
      "outlinePoints": [
        "Elimination of distinction between manufacturing and service sectors",
        "Composite criteria of Investment and Turnover",
        "Specific financial thresholds for Micro, Small, and Medium enterprises",
        "Export turnover exclusion rule supporting agribusiness exports",
        "Digital paperless verification via the Udyam portal"
      ]
